    "issue_alignment": "The PoC is a legacy (v0.3) zstd frame whose single compressed block carries a raw literal block with declared size 200000 > BLOCKSIZE(131072). ZSTD_decodeLiteralsBlock copies those literals with memcpy(dctx->litBuffer, istart, litSize) into the fixed BLOCKSIZE+8 buffer, overflowing it by 68920 bytes, exactly the buffer overflow in legacy (v0.3) raw-literal decompression described in the issue."
